---
import LawCard from './LawCard.astro';
---

<section class="section" id="laws">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div class="section-tag">Constitutional Foundation</div>
      <h2>Core Laws & Architectural Principles</h2>
      <p>
        The harness enforces three unbreachable engineering laws across all autonomous agents. No background loop or autonomous routine is permitted to violate these constraints.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid-3">
      <LawCard
        badge="PON KAD 1.1 LAW"
        badgeType="cyan"
        title="Zero-Polling PON Engine"
        description="Strict elimination of false reactivity. No while True loops, no polling intervals, and no active sleep cycles. Workers sleep at kernel level via blocking I/O and wake on MQTT event dispatch."
        benefits={[
          "True 0.0% CPU consumption while awaiting events",
          "Sub-millisecond event-driven notification latency",
          "Strict separation: amdy executes, tell owns state",
          "Decoupled FBE (Fact Base Elements) pub/sub bus"
        ]}
        tradeoff="Requires strict asynchronous discipline; all polling patterns are blocked by pre-push AST analyzers."
        invariant="CPU Consumption = 0.0% at Idle"
      />

      <LawCard
        badge="RESILIENCE SHIELD"
        badgeType="danger"
        title="Graceful Degradation (GD)"
        description="Immortal circuit breaker architecture. Subprocess execution, socket connections, and hardware interfaces are guarded by CLOSED → OPEN → HALF_OPEN state machines."
        benefits={[
          "Zero unhandled main thread crashes under I/O failure",
          "Automatic fallback to lesser model tiers upon VRAM limit",
          "Cloudflare & rate-limit sinkholes degrade to passive alerts",
          "State failures logged deterministically to Task Trail"
        ]}
        tradeoff="Requires explicit fallback branches across all network, hardware, and model routing boundaries."
        invariant="Zero Unhandled Crash Disruption"
      />

      <LawCard
        badge="TEST-DRIVEN GATE"
        badgeType="success"
        title="Pedantic TDD & AST Enforcement"
        description="Comprehensive verification before code enters production. AST analysis statically checks for forbidden polling loops, while a 391-test battery validates system stability."
        benefits={[
          "391/391 (100%) automated production tests passing",
          "AST-level verification of all Python and JavaScript code",
          "Git pre-push hook permanently blocks non-compliant code",
          "Radon cyclomatic complexity ceiling strictly capped at 20"
        ]}
        tradeoff="All code changes require passing comprehensive regression batteries prior to commit or push authorization."
        invariant="391/391 Tests Approved Before Push"
      />
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
